# FAST profile for the simulator (GO at up to 20 m/s, 8 m/s^2, 55 deg lean -- raised 2026-10-15 for the PN GO)
# FAST profile for the simulator (sim_up.sh --fast): lets a GO dash fly a steep straight line at its full speed.
# The descent limit is what held a 5 m/s GO to 2.2 m/s: a straight line from 12 m up to a target ~13 m away descends
# ~0.75 m per metre flown, and ArduPilot slows the whole line so the descent stays within WP_SPD_DN.
# Real aircraft: these are flight-safety settings -- choose them deliberately (fast descents risk vortex ring state).
# horizontal speed m/s (default 10)
WP_SPD 20
# descent m/s (default 1.5)
WP_SPD_DN 6
# climb m/s (default 2.5)
WP_SPD_UP 5
# horizontal acceleration m/s/s (default 2.5)
WP_ACC 8
# jerk m/s/s/s (default 1)
WP_JERK 10
# tilt limit, degrees (default 30): more tilt = harder acceleration and a higher top speed
ATC_ANGLE_MAX 55
# how fast acceleration may change, m/s/s/s (default 5): measured, the drone took ~1.7 s to tilt to 30 deg after GO
PSC_NE_JERK 25
# vertical acceleration for ABORT's climb-away (default 1; 3 above): measured, an ABORT during a fast descent kept sinking
# ~4 m (6.6 -> 2.6 m) for 2 s while the descent was braked at 3 m/s/s
WP_ACC_Z 5
PSC_D_JERK 15
